\title{epiworldRcalibrate: calibrate agent-based epidemic models in seconds}
\description{
The package calibrates the SEIR and SIR agent-based models of
\pkg{epiworldR} from daily counts, with DeepIMC (a trained bidirectional
LSTM) or four standard methods, and works with whole curves and
interventions.
}
\details{
The main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=calibrate_window]{calibrate_window()}}: one window of daily counts, with \code{"DeepIMC"},
\code{"ABC_SMC"}, \code{"ABC_MCMC"}, \code{"DE"} or \code{"NELDERMEAD"}, for SEIR or SIR.
\item \code{\link[=calibrate_curve]{calibrate_curve()}}: a whole curve, with or without smoothing and with or
without splitting it where its growth rate changes (\code{\link[=split_curve]{split_curve()}},
\code{\link[=smooth_cases]{smooth_cases()}}).
\item \code{\link[=recover_curve]{recover_curve()}}: the epidemic the estimates imply, run again with the
agent-based model, and its plot (with the known measures marked).
\item \code{\link[=find_intervention]{find_intervention()}} and \code{\link[=intervention_effect]{intervention_effect()}}: the breakpoint that
follows a known measure, and the cases expected without it.
\item \code{\link[=predict_cases]{predict_cases()}}, \code{\link[=coverage]{coverage()}}, \code{\link[=interval_score]{interval_score()}}: bands and scores.
\item Data: \link{outbreak_data}, \link{covid_waves_2020}, \link{interventions},
\link{flu_baltimore_1918}, \link{covid_utah}, \link{admissions_utah}, \link{covid_us_states},
\link{disease_parameters} and \code{\link[=known_values]{known_values()}}.
}

See the vignettes: \code{vignette("calibrating-windows")},
